# Game Hub

Hub = Next.js App Router (`app/`, `lib/`). Games = separate folders under `games/` registered in `games/registry.ts`. Three.js from npm inside game packages.

Read `docs/architecture.md` before large changes. API contract: `openapi/openapi.yaml` — update it when HTTP behavior changes.

## Must

- Keep games out of HTML strings / CDN script tags.
- Gate game UI and game APIs with active account (or admin) via `canAccessGames` / `requireActivePlayer`.
- `AUTH_URL` is site origin only (`http://localhost:3000`), never the Google callback path.
- Prefer extending `lib/gifts.ts` actions + registry over one-off gift hacks.
- Leave `legacy/` as reference; do not build new features there.

## Must not

- Multi-instance Redis SSE unless explicitly requested.
- Payments / Discord unlock / packaging `.exe` unless requested.
- Copy or resell third-party Discord games into this tree.

## Next.js

This Next version may differ from training data. Check `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` and root `AGENTS.md` before using unfamiliar APIs.
